virglrenderer: Venus attachment formats are ones the device renders to

What: render pass attachments (vkCreateRenderPass and 2), and the color,
depth and stencil formats of a pipeline's dynamic rendering and of a
secondary's inherited rendering, are formats vkr's format table knows with
the color or depth/stencil attachment feature among the host's linear or
optimal tiling features (VK_FORMAT_UNDEFINED, no attachment, where Vulkan
allows it), and a color format list has the count's entries. A refused
create or begin ends the app's context.
Why: an unknown VkFormat in a pipeline's rendering info ended both drivers
(KosmicKrisp in kk_lower_nir; MoltenVK: strlen(NULL) in
MVKPixelFormats::getMTLPixelFormat), and KosmicKrisp ended on an
R64G64B64A64 color attachment, which Metal has no pixel format for.
Upstream: OmacVM policy (spec VUIDs), draft only.
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-venus-commands.c (p-gfx-format-, p-gfx-depth-format-,
r-format-, c-inherit-format-bad cases).

